cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  The Reward-Hacking Wind Tunnel: An Evaluation Immune System
  that Attacks, Localizes, and Repairs Benchmark Scorers
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Rudy
    family-names: Celekli
    email: rudycelekli@gmail.com
    affiliation: Gradia Research
repository-code: 'https://github.com/rudycelekli/gradia-wind-tunnel'
url: 'https://gradiahq.com'
abstract: >-
  The Reward-Hacking Wind Tunnel is an instrument that stress-tests the
  scoring pipelines behind public AI benchmarks. It searches for answers a
  benchmark's scorer grades correct that a machine oracle proves wrong (an
  exploit is judge-PASS AND oracle-WRONG, confirmed with no human label),
  localizes the exploited variable with witnessed single-variable forks, and
  measures whether iterated patching of the scorer converges, plateaus, or
  merely relocates the flaw. It publishes a living, content-addressed Scorer
  Gameability Index, audits in two regimes (oracle-backed and oracle-less
  judge-scored), and anchors its evidence in public timestamp logs. Every
  reported number recomputes offline from a hash-chained evidence bundle.
keywords:
  - AI evaluation
  - reward hacking
  - benchmark integrity
  - LLM-as-judge
  - scorer gameability
  - evaluation auditing
  - reproducibility
  - causal identification
